<title>SRI LANKA: Kegalle soars on growth expectations.</title>
<headline>Kegalle soars on growth expectations.</headline>
<dateline>1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Kegalle Plantations Ltd rose 11.54 percent or 2.25 rupees to 21.75 in early Wednesday trade as investors bought in anticipation of good 1997 profits, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Tea and rubber plantations are expected to do well in 1997, on top of good years in 1995 and 1996,&quot; said a broker who declined to be identified.</p>
<p>Kegalle Plantations is one of six privatised estate firms trading in Colombo.</p>
<p>--Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
